.TH HTTP_SOCKET_WRITE 3
.SH NAME
http_socket_write \- write operation of the output buffer of an HTTP client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "ssize_t http_socket_write(fd_type " fd ", void* " buf ", size_t " len ", buffer* " b ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_socket_write ()
is the operation of
.IR h->q.out ,
where the http structure is
.IR b->cookie .
It writes with send(2) or tls_write(3). A TLS write that has to wait for the network gives -1 with errno EAGAIN
or EWOULDBLOCK. Like
.BR http_socket_read (3)
it updates the status of the response when the connection is closed or fails.
.BR http_body_flush (3)
calls it directly.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of bytes written, 0 if the connection was closed, -1 on an error or when the write has to wait.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_socket(3), http_body_flush(3)
